 <s> sw lat1   x6   | M3 latch deleted; d2 "|= BIT"  | COUNT of this site's
                    |     removed                    |   message: 1 vs 2 vs 0
 <s> lw surv   x6   | M1 (len!=8 && writeflag ==     | process exit status; a
                    |     MEM_WRITE) -- the clause-  |   len=4 READ falls to the
                    |     (d) canonical if(X)->      |   still-live READ kill
                    |     if(X && Y)                 |
 <s> accept    x6   | guard-growth (the de-escalation| the arm's own debug() line
                    |     accept side); guard-only   |   for a LEGAL len=8 write,
                    |     form -- see note below     |   present vs absent
 xsite 6msg         | M2 latch-bit collision /       | COUNT of DISTINCT site
                    |     shared latch               |   messages: 6 vs fewer
 xsite order        | ANCHOR (clause f): attribution | the SEQUENCE of messages
                    |     to a SPECIFIC window       |   vs the issue order
 ld readkill        | CONTRACT: a round that silently| exit1 plus "TODO: read
                    |     removed the READ kills     |   from" text still present
 other kill         | CONTRACT: the :372 straggler   | exit1 outside all six
                    |     still fatal                |   windows

 GROWTH-MUTANT FORM for the accept rows: the latch operand is a per-site
 COMPILE-TIME CONSTANT the guard cannot feed, so guard-only widening is
 NON-EQUIVALENT and quieter than joint -- by the discriminator, guard-only is the
 form to build.  Mutant: `len != 8` -> `len != 8 || (relative_addr & 8)`, a
 plausible "tighten to 16-byte alignment" edit.

 *** ACCEPT ROWS ARE THEREFORE PROBED AT AN OFFSET WITH BIT 3 SET, or the growth
     mutant cannot redden them.  That is a row-DESIGN consequence derived HERE,
     before the table: an accept row at +0x00 would be green under its own growth
     mutant, i.e. vacuous by construction. ***

 ANCHOR CHECK (clause f), in its own words: "if every window's message were
 attributed to the WRONG window, which row reds?"  -> `xsite order`, and only it.
 Without it the six per-site rows run in six SEPARATE sessions, and each would pass
 if the code emitted ANY site's message, because only one site is touched per
 session.

