================================================================================

D1.  THE PROBE MUST BE WIRED INTO A GATE, OR CARRY A DATED EXEMPTION.
     tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py enforces that every committed detector
     under regress/ is RUN by a gate.  Its header records the failure it was
     built after: SIXTY-SIX detector rows across four rounds defended nothing
     between batteries because no gate ran them, and no gate, check or ledger
     field could say so.  Committing sgi_re_width_probe.py to regress/ WITHOUT a
     gate call reproduces exactly that.
     The naming convention already matches the tree (asic_badaddr_probe.py,
     gdrom_cond_probe.py), and the invocation shape gates use is
        python3 <name>_probe.py "$BIN" > "$LOG" 2>&1 || true
     followed by count/check rows against $LOG.

D2.  *** THE ROW COUNT HAS TWO DIFFERENT RIGHT ANSWERS, AND THEY MUST NOT BE
     CONFLATED -- this is the counts rule applied before anyone writes one down. ***
        10  row() CALL SITES     -- what check_probe_wiring.py counts, via ast
        35  EMITTED rows         -- what the probe prints and what OPUS497T_RESULT
                                    denominates
     They differ because four call sites sit inside a `for' loop over the six
     SITES, and one more loops for the ld-kill rows.  Deriver for the first:
        python -c "import ast,io;t=ast.parse(io.open(F).read());print(sum(1 for n
        in ast.walk(t) if isinstance(n,ast.Call) and getattr(n.func,'id','')=='row'))"
     Deriver for the second: the OPUS497T_RESULT denominator in any preserved log.
     check_probe_wiring.py's own header warns about precisely this shape -- its
     first census used a grep and silently dropped every control row that was not
     R-prefixed.  A round record saying "35 rows" next to a checker reporting 10
     is not a contradiction; it is two units, and each must name its deriver.

D3.  est/ PROPAGATION IS OWED.  dev_sgi_re.c is NOT in tools/est_divergence.txt
     (re-derived: that file lists SIX paths, and CLAUDE.md's prose says SEVEN --
     flagged, not resolved, since it is not this round's file to correct).  est/'s
     copy is byte-identical to SEC's today (both md5 01f5a74064b9f96127d9fcca01bdd03a),
     so precommit_check.sh section A will require the fix to land in BOTH trees
     byte-identically.
     *** A METHOD WARNING FROM MY OWN SESSION: I first "checked" this with
     `grep -c ... && ... cmp -s ... && echo IDENTICAL || echo differs' and it
     printed "est differs or absent" -- because grep -c returning 0 EXITS 1 and
     short-circuited the whole chain, so THE cmp NEVER RAN.  The md5s settled it.
     A && chain reports the first failure as though it were the last test's
     answer; do not put a test after a counter in one chain. ***

